  "question": {
    "text": "A Zener diode having break down voltage $\\mathrm{Vz}=6 \\mathrm{~V}$ is used in a voltage regulator circuit as shown in the figure. The minimum current required to pass through the Zener to act as a voltage regulator is $10 \\mathrm{~mA}$ and maximum allowed current through Zener is $40 \\mathrm{~mA}$. The maximum value of $R_{\\mathrm{s}}$ for Zener to act as a voltage regulator is\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/wbjee/LQ4Ex1Lm3fBBtrw0_24bOpfvtHYdA-zy-gcbPNbX72o.original.fullsize.png\">",
